ators that generate Glassmorphism CSS for you. Here are some popular ones: Glass UI, Glassmorphism CSS Generator by Hype4 Academy, and Glassmorphism CSS Effect Generator."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How to make glassmorphism in figma?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"To create a glassmorphism effect in Figma, follow these steps:</p><p>Start by creating a shape or container for your design element.Apply a translucent background color with a subtle blur effect.Add a subtle inner shadow to simulate glass depth.Finally, experiment with opacity and gradient effects to enhance the glassy appearance."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How to create glassmorphism?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"To create glassmorphism, you can follow these steps:</p><p>Start by designing a sleek, minimalist user interface.Use transparent backgrounds with frosted glass effects.Apply soft shadows and gradients to mimic the glassy appearance.Maintain consistency in the overall design to achieve a harmonious glassmorphic effect."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is glassmorphism design?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Glassmorphism design is a modern UI trend that creates a frosted glass effect on elements. It adds depth and transparency, resembling frosted glass, elevating the overall aesthetic. This style promotes a visually appealing and user-friendly interface."}}]},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"VideoObject","name":"I created Neumorphism, Glassmorphism and Aurora","description":"Hi! You voted, I complied :-) Here's my video about how I created Neumorphism, Glassmorphism and Aurora via very popular Medium articles. I've been writing about UX and UI design there for a long time, and in 2019 my first trend caught on, creating a worldwide naming convention.","thumbnailUrl":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/SdcyDZbFYFU/default.jpg","uploadDate":"2021-05-24","duration":"PT12M40S","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"LambdaTest","logo":{"@type":"ImageO